73:The well-known {\sc Disjoint Paths} problem is to decide if a graph contains $k$ pairwise disjoint paths, each connecting a different terminal pair from a set of $k$ distinct pairs.
74:We determine, with an exception of two cases, the complexity of the {\sc Disjoint Paths} problem for $H$-free graphs. 
75:If $k$ is fixed, we obtain the {\sc $k$-Disjoint Paths} problem, which is known to be polynomial-time solvable on the class of all graphs for every $k\geq 1$.
