90:Karp~\cite{Ka75} proved that {\sc Disjoint Paths} is \NP-complete. If $k$ is fixed, that is, not part of the input, then we denote the problem as {\sc $k$-Disjoint Paths}. For every $k\geq 1$, Robertson and Seymour proved the following celebrated result.
