99:As {\sc Disjoint Paths} is \NP-complete, it is natural to consider special graph classes. The {\sc Disjoint Paths} problem is known to be \NP-complete even for graph of clique-width at most~$6$~\cite{GW06}, split graphs~\cite{HHLS15}, interval graphs~\cite{NS96} and line graphs. The latter result can be obtained by a straightforward reduction (see, for example,~\cite{GW06,HHLS15}) from its edge variant, {\sc Edge Disjoint Paths}, proven to be \NP-complete by Even, Itai and Shamir~\cite{EIS76}. On the positive side, {\sc Disjoint Paths} is polynomial-time solvable for cographs, or equivalently, $P_4$-free graphs~\cite{GW06}. 
