+Worst-case NP-completeness does not make this generated distribution hard. Its displayed clause blocks are XOR equations, so exact Gaussian elimination over GF(2) solves the shipping system in (O(V^3)). Across the eight self-test seeds it used about 128,000 XOR/pivot operations and 0.04 seconds for (V=192), succeeding 8/8 as expected. The compact route notices that the CHECK rows encode (I+T+T^{n/2}) on one cycle. For power-of-two (n), its inverse is (T^{n/2-2}+T^{n-2}+T^{n-1}); applying that identity and reversing the linear XOR gates costs 224 XORs. This large mechanical/compact gap is the Track B claim. It is deliberately disclosed rather than mislabeled as structural hardness.
 
