codex
Implemented and locally verified the Track B generator.

- Generator: [gen_2105_06349.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2105.06349/gen_2105_06349.py:27)
- Gate evidence: [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2105.06349/selftest_report.json)
- Documentation: [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2105.06349/README.md:1)
- Oracle transcript: [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2105.06349/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- G9 transcripts: [structural](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2105.06349/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl), [placebo](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2105.06349/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The family uses the paper’s Lemma 4 construction from satisfiable 3-CNF to 2-Disjoint Connected Subgraphs on claw-free line graphs. Track B is required because this generated XOR subdistribution admits \(O(V^3)\) Gaussian elimination; the compact structural route takes 224 XORs. The paper confirms fixed-\(k\) Disjoint Paths is polynomial and provides the relevant line-graph hardness construction. [Official paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2105.06349)

Local results:

- All mandatory local gates pass.
- Guessing: 0/200,000; exact density \(2^{-32}\).
- Five attacks: each 0/8.
- Gaussian reference: 8/8, approximately 127,535 operations.
- G8: 300/300 transformations invariant and valid.
- Answer: 96 characters, 32 atoms.
- Intended route: 224 operations.

The result is not yet submission-ready: `harden.py` was run, but OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” on every redraw. The transcripts honestly retain those script-generated errors; no hardness verdict was fabricated. Once the OpenRouter key limit is raised, the bare and two G9 runs must be repeated.
